"Don't send Connection-Allowlist reports for history navigations" (crbugs
581211928 and 572312779, not public; no CVE listed yet): for a session
history navigation, the URL checked against the initiator's
Connection-Allowlist (enabled by default) comes from the history entry, so
any page could use history.go(-n) with a report-only policy to learn the
full URLs of the other pages in its tab's history from the violation
reports; the LoadingPredictor's speculative requests leaked the same way.
chromium/src main commit 8bc20d0797fdbb892973f3f1cd1ff9e8bc5489ce
(main@{#1732572}), merged on 2026-11-04 to the 157 branch
(78eb1330142f521a3638bfd5b573ec448ea8792b, refs/branch-heads/8103@{#1125},
after the 157.0.8103.45 tag). This is the 157 merge without its tests.
Drop it once a 157 tag has it.

